  "changes": [
    "Composed official USD visual geometry; no modeled substitute and no mesh decimation.",
    "Baked original mesh transforms, retained authored face-corner normals, UVs, material subsets and PreviewSurface PBR texture bindings.",
    "Triangulated original polygons for glTF; generated tangent basis for normal-map portability.",
    "Centered horizontal bounds and grounded minimum height at zero; converted Z-up USD to Y-up glTF in meters.",
    "Resampled texture images to maximum 512 pixels and embedded all PNG textures in GLB.",
    "Converted PreviewSurface to glTF metallic-roughness; preserved texture transforms including 30x ORM mapping for decals.",
    "Removed runtime-specific USD/MDL representation and non-visual USD metadata from the web rendering artifact.",
    "No geometry shape fabrication, substitutions, retopology, physical solver implementation or certification performed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Visual conversion only: GLB does not preserve USDPhysics/PhysX/MuJoCo/Newton variants, collision schemas, mass/friction metadata, semantic label schemas, nonvisual sensor material schemas or SimReady conformance.",
    "Original packages and original conformance evidence are retained separately; package conformance does not certify this GLB as SimReady. Historical USD metadata also includes failed profile requirements; no current physics validation has been run.",
    "The upstream cardboard trim material binds its normal input to the trim ORM image. This source binding is deliberately preserved rather than silently corrected.",
    "Original OmniPBR source files import standard MDL and NVIDIA core_definitions runtime modules. They are preserved in upstream, but GLB uses PreviewSurface instead; no MDL runtime is shipped or required.",
    "Round-trip renders use neutral QA lights and will not pixel-match NVIDIA thumbnails or other render engines."
  ],
